      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To create a compelling contrast to your intellectual detective, consider introducing characters who embody a raw, emotional, and intuitive approach to crime. A ruthless gang leader or mafia enforcer with a volatile temper, perhaps one who acts solely on instinct rather than logic, could bring a sense of danger and unpredictability to the story. Alternatively, a sly and charismatic con artist could serve as a foil, using charm and emotional manipulation to get what they want, while your detective must rely on cold calculation to outsmart them. These characters would challenge the detective's principles and force him to confront the darker aspects of human nature.",
